From: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:46:47 -0400
Subject: [graphite] Include hairline and subpixel strokes in inflation radius

Clarifies that `Shape::getInflationRadius` applies only to regular
strokes and not hairlines. Adds asserts to catch the unexpected case
where CoverBoundsRenderStep would hit w/o being a regular stroke.

Logic in ClipStack's draw bounds calculations is cleaned up to either
handle the fill path (no outset, or 1/2 local pixel outset if it's
subpixel), or the stroke/hairline path. The stroke/hairline path is
merged now by using the local pixel width as the minimum local stroke
width. Hairlines and subpixel strokes are automatically expanded to
this, which simplifies some of the conditions from the old code.

By handling hairlines this way, they get now take into account the rest
of the join and cap styling's impact on their local bounds. This is most
significant for hairlines with large miter limits.

A small change with this is that when we add the local AA outset for
subpixel fills, subpixel strokes, and hairlines, the old code outset by
a full pixel on each axis. This CL changes it to be half a pixel
(locally conservative), which is sufficient given the ClipStack's
implicit 1/2px outset allowance already.

